# Cloudberry's gpcloud regression schedule (gpcontrib/gpcloud/regress/
# regress_schedule) on the port, against the suite's S3 (run.sh): each test
# of the schedule, in its order, and whether it runs here --
#
#   run  <test>
#   skip <test>  why not
#
# A skipped test reads a data set of Cloudberry's own, in its bucket
# s3test.pivotal.io, which is not public and which the suite does not make
# for its size -- stock ticks of 31 million rows (normal/, 1.3 GB), the
# airline data of five GB a file, their gzipped and deflated copies -- or
# asks for what only Amazon's S3 does.  The data a test that runs reads is
# s3data.py's.  1_19_proxy and 5_02_normal_https_param are not in the
# schedule, and are not run here either.

